pve-cloudprovision (1.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * POST /nodes/{node}/qemu/{vmid}/cloudprovision/ipconfig (CLI sync-ipconfig):
    derive the cloud-init IP config of every network device from its current
    routed IPs again and regenerate the cloud-init drive.

 -- yuant <me@yuant.cc>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0800

pve-cloudprovision (1.0.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: create cloud servers from the QEMU templates of the
    cluster with CPU, memory, system and data disks and any number of network
    devices, each with routed IPs (pve-routedip), rate limit, traffic quota
    (pve-trafficd) and the guest IP config derived from the routed IPs
    (cloud-init); reinstall with a new template keeping the settings; clone
    and migrate templates on local storage of other nodes; API
    (/nodes/{node}/cloudprovision), CLI (pve-cloudprovision) and web UI.

 -- yuant <me@yuant.cc>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:15:00 +0800
